[
    {
        "content": "<p>If a command macro partially matches some syntax but then parsing fails, the macro will still generate a command from the syntax elements that were matched.  This seems undesirable - is there any way to prevent this?</p>\n<p>To make this concrete, consider this macro:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">declare_syntax_cat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"bar\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"&lt;\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Map \"bar x &lt; 1 2 3 &gt;\" to \"def bar x := [1, 2, 3]\".</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">macro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">])</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Macro</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">throwError</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"foo\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>It works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">-- prints [1, 2, 3]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>However, now consider this bogus input:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">-- prints [1, 2, 3]  ?!?</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Despite the fact that the syntax is malformed, the macro still generates a definition.  Can this be prevented?</p>",
        "id": 618001535,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1787339408
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh, this seems like a bug to me. <span aria-label=\"eyes\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f440\" role=\"img\" title=\"eyes\">:eyes:</span></p>",
        "id": 618001913,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1787339540
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(To minimize, the <code>declare_syntax_cat</code> is not load-bearing; <code>syntax (name := foo) \"bar\" ...</code> reproduces the bug too.)</p>",
        "id": 618002178,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1787339632
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, to make the example minimal I could just have written</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"bar\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"&lt;\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I'm happy to file a bug if there is consensus that this is a bug, and it is not already known.  Do other macro gurus have an opinion?</p>",
        "id": 618004261,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1787340311
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note, interestingly I think there are two potential bugs here:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>the macro firing at all(? not sure if this is intentional, but it's surprising)</li>\n<li>the match, which allows <code>Syntax.missing</code> to match <code>&gt;</code> (There's already behavior where nonreserved symbols are similarly not matched, but I don't thiiiink that applies here?)</li>\n</ol>",
        "id": 618005792,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1787340841
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, wait, (1) is not a bug per se because of things like dot-completion, which require elaboration to proceed despite a parse error (so that we can e.g. modify the infotrees)</p>",
        "id": 618006353,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1787341030
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hmmm, and possibly that means the behavior in 2 is load-bearing as well...</p>",
        "id": 618006599,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1787341121
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>One thing you can do manually is just to check for <code>hasMissing</code>, and arguably there are different options here; the simple one is just to say the macro doesn't apply:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Syntax</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"s2\">\"bar\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"&lt;\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">macro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">hasMissing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Macro</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">throwUnsupported</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">])</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Macro</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">throwUnsupported</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- not found</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>or, you could create it with <code>sorry</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Syntax</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"s2\">\"bar\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"&lt;\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"&gt;\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">macro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">hasMissing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span><span class=\"o\">])</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">])</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Macro</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">throwUnsupported</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- `y` exists, but we abort due to sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The latter is what e.g. <code>def</code> does if it encounters a parse error (say, <code>def y := [1,2,</code>).</p>",
        "id": 618008430,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1787341783
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>A manual check with <code>hasMissing</code> seems to work well - that's great.  Thanks for the useful suggestion!</p>",
        "id": 618025600,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1787349665
    }
]